An owner requests an architect to design a new family house.
An owner reviews the proposed blueprint before approving the final design.
An owner submits a permit application to the city for construction approval.

An architect creates a detailed blueprint for the house based on the owner’s requirements.
An architect reviews the city’s construction guidelines before finalizing the design.
An architect updates the blueprint after the city requests design adjustments.

A city officer reviews the permit application to ensure the project meets zoning laws.
A city officer issues a construction permit after approving the architect’s plans.
A city officer visits the construction site to prepare an inspection report.

A construction overseer from an instruction company hires construction workers after receiving the permit.
A construction overseer orders materials according to the architect’s blueprint.
A construction overseer updates the project schedule after delays on the site.

A construction worker lays the foundation following the overseer’s instructions.
A construction worker assembles walls and installs beams based on the blueprint.
A construction worker reports a safety concern to the overseer for resolution.